# test_runner

This is a simple application, intended to eventually be the in-tree test runner
application for basic tests like xpcshell and mochitests on iOS.

## Building

The `TestRunner.app` bundle will be built by mozbuild during the normal build
process, and can be found in `$(TOPOBJDIR)/dist/TestRunner.app`.

This approach was taken rather than using an xcode project to make it easier to
integrate into the existing mozbuild build system.

## Installing and Running on Simulator

Install the TestRunner.app into the currently booted simulator. The `booted`
argument can be replaced by a simulator identifier to specify a specific
simulator.

```
$ xcrun simctl install booted path/to/objdir/dist/TestRunner.app
```

Run the installed TestRunner.app, optionally passing in arguments, and routing
console output to the current console for debugging purposes.

```
$ xcrun simctl launch --console booted org.mozilla.TestRunner <argv>...
```

You can also pass `-w` to cause the application to pause until a debugger is
connected. The command will log the pid of the application as it is starting so
you can attach a debugger (e.g. from xcode).

## Installing and Running on Device

As of the time of writing, this has not yet been tested on an actual device. In
order to do so, you'll need to build with a non-simulator target, and codesign
the TestRunner.app bundle with a command like:

```
$ codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=identifier,entitlements,resource-rules path/to/objdir/dist/TestRunner.app
```

Then you'll need to find a way to push the .app to the device to install & run
it. I unfortunately haven't put in the effort to find the xcode commands to do
this yet.

## TODO

This is very much an early POC of the design. There's currently no support for
building for real devices (the Info.plist is hardcoded to simulator), and it
doesn't actually do anything yet other than display a basic webpage.

The intention is that this application should eventually support being
configured by our test runners to be a mochitest test runner, xpcshell test
runner, or similar.

It loads and starts the application through the experimental `geckoview`
Objective-C API, to keep it more similar to the API we intend to expose to
embedders.
